{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/con/skills/pulls/23","id":4834785792,"node_id":"PR_kwDORUy0bs8AAAABICz6AA","html_url":"https://github.com/con/skills/pull/23","diff_url":"https://github.com/con/skills/pull/23.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/con/skills/pull/23.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/con/skills/issues/23","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/con/skills/pulls/23/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/con/skills/pulls/23/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/con/skills/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/con/skills/issues/23/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/con/skills/statuses/15da761f63a5a45c507e6596a549720bd43a1e84","number":23,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add assess-stamped and align-stamped skills","user":{"login":"asmacdo","id":1028657,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjg2NTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1028657?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmacdo","html_url":"https://github.com/asmacdo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmacdo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmacdo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmacdo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmacdo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmacdo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmacdo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmacdo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmacdo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmacdo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Two skills for applying the [STAMPED principles](https://stamped-principles.org/) to existing projects, as proposed in stamped-principles/stamped-agent-skills#3. They live here first so we can use them and reuse this repo's CI and conventions; whatever proves useful can move to stamped-principles/stamped-agent-skills later, possibly with an automatic sync.\n\n- **assess-stamped**: profiles what a project does or plans to do, answers every item of the published checklist yes/no/unknown with evidence labelled as inspection or execution (cheap, non-destructive probes only; never a full re-run), and lists the gaps, MUST items first. It is read-only and writes a markdown report.\n- **align-stamped**: assesses first, then writes one STAMPED section into whatever agent harness the project already has (`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, spec-kit constitution), sized to the project's goals. For each gap it offers options with tradeoffs, always including the smallest change, and without prescribing tools.\n\nBoth link the version-pinned principles and checklist JSON rather than paraphrasing them. Three earlier assessors paraphrased them and drifted.\n\nEach skill's `DESIGN.md` records the scope decisions and the work deliberately left as separate drop-ins (structured JSON output and a checklist share link, hands-on reproduction, `create-stamped-project`, a generated condensed STAMPED context). The report is plain markdown for now: the checklist UI's schema only records a reason for a `no`, and an assessment needs evidence for every answer.\n\n**Verified**: `ci/validate_skills.py` passes for both (0 errors, 0 warnings). Neither skill has been run on a real project yet. The first planned target is dandi/compression-comparisons-t261-study.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-12T20:44:18Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T18:37:10Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"asmacdo:stamped-skills","ref":"stamped-skills","repo":{"id":1416111919,"node_id":"R_kgDOVGgnLw","name":"ski